messages:
Maya: Quick q — when an fncall returns invalid JSON (array instead of object) and the orchestrator routes to a degenerate fallback, how should the console and telemetry surface the reason? Right now we just show 'fallback: true' and SREs are opening tickets for 'unknown fallback'.
Sam: We do write validator.reason into internal logs but don’t expose it to the UI because of PII concerns.
Eli: The core ask from platform teams: a small, safe signal that explains 'why' (enum) + an opt-in redacted hint for debugging. Not raw payload.
Harper: Also: billing attribution — if a request falls back we currently bill the fallback route. That both skews quotas and frustrates product owners. We should preserve the original route for quota/billing when fallback is validation-triggered.
Maya: @Sam can we add a non-PII enum like VALIDATION_ARRAY_ROOT or MISSING_FIELD to the response metadata? UI can surface it without exposing payload.
Sam: Possibly. Needs proto change + RBAC on whether hint gets shown. We should avoid putting any raw text into logs unless sampled.
ci-bot: validator-service v3.4.2 reported: fncall validation error at 12:23: "root type mismatch" — sampling=on
Eli: Draft proposal: include metadata.validation_code (enum) in InvokeResponse and metadata.validation_hint (short redacted snippet) only returned when caller has admin scope or when sampling flag is set. Telemetry should emit validation_code as a tag so dashboards can trend reasons.
Harper: Console UX idea: show a compact pill — "fell back: validation=ARRAY_ROOT" with a disclosure arrow that reads "show redacted sample (audit only)" and a link to open an eval test to reproduce. No raw payload inline.
Maya: For rollouts, can we make validation_code visible only for canary slices (opt-in)? Teams want to run stricter validators on canary traffic before enabling for everyone.
Sam: Implementation notes: 1) add enum to proto, 2) wire validation_code through router + orchestrator response, 3) add server-side sampling for returning redacted_hint, 4) console flag + RBAC, 5) update billing pipeline to prefer original_route for accounting when validation_code != NONE.
Eli: Proto sketch: ```proto
message InvokeResponse {
  enum ValidationCode {
    NONE = 0;
    ARRAY_ROOT = 1;
    MISSING_REQUIRED_FIELD = 2;
    TYPE_MISMATCH = 3;
    MALFORMED_JSON = 4;
  }
  ValidationCode validation_code = 20;
  // short redacted hint, returned only under sampling/admin scope
  string redacted_hint = 21;
  // existing fields...
}
```
Harper: Security note: redacted_hint must run through secret detection and be scrubbed; also add a short TTL for audit retrieval. Engage red-team before enabling sample payload return.
Maya: Action items: Sam - prototype proto + APi gating; Eli - add telemetry tag + console telemetry dashboard mock; Harper - mock console affordance & security checklist; Maya - update rollout playbook to include canary opt-in for validation visibility.
Sam: I'll open a tracking PR with the proto diff and a design doc for billing implications, ETA EOW.
Eli: I'll add a Prometheus counter + trace tag: invoke.validation_code. Sampling/retention in infra triage.
Harper: I'll sketch the UI and send screenshots to #design and #security for quick feedback.
Maya: Thanks all :thumbsup:
